  <content>
  <section><title>Getting Ready for Unit 8</title>
<para>To be ready for this unit, you need to be able to:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Write equivalent expressions using the distributive property. </item>
  <item> Find the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph of a quadratic equation given in factored form. </item>
  <item> Match quadratic graphs and their functions. </item>
</list>
<para>Next, you will answer some questions that will help you see how ready you are for this unit. If you need help, some mini-lessons will help you brush up on anything you need to work on.</para></section>
</content>
</document>
